Minister Valerius Vane is a high-ranking member of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] and sits on the Calarian council. He is [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]]'s friend and former owner: Arctos says he was Vane's pet before the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] gave him speech and reason, that he saved Vane's life from a band of [[Org/RunGunners/index|RunGunners]], and that the two are equals now.

Vane's home is a gated three-story marble manor in the residential north of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]], its walls carved with the family crest, a V with a sword through it. Its majordomo is [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley Hart]]. The Vane family keeps no [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] in the house, and holds that Hearts should not run all of society, though they still use them in their work.

In the manor's reading room hang two paintings, a small acrylic of a coastline and a long panorama of the Aurideon skyline by [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]], one of the family's patronized artists. The panorama does not show the [[Pharos]], though the paint there is raised as if something had been painted over.

Vane is about thirty-five, and [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] has served the family longer than Vane has been alive. He carries a small piece of palladium set near his heart, paired with a Palladium Rod kept in the manor, so that the household learns if his body is badly hurt. He keeps a couch in his office at the Templar Indictum for the nights he stays at the council.

Vane has been kept at the council for days by an uproar over something that happened at a meeting. In his absence [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] let Arctos take the Quinn panorama, one of the minister's favourites, to [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]].
